WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.290 --> 00:00:03.590
INTRO:
Within just 2 years of launching, this platform

00:00:03.590 --> 00:00:09.719
became the world’s largest social media
network eventually surpassing over 100 million

00:00:09.719 --> 00:00:10.719
users.

00:00:10.719 --> 00:00:16.150
Within 3 years, this website become the most
visited website in the US surpassing even

00:00:16.150 --> 00:00:18.120
Yahoo and Google.

00:00:18.120 --> 00:00:22.560
Given this explosive growth, I don’t think
you’d be surprised to hear that this platform

00:00:22.560 --> 00:00:27.420
was acquired for $580 million within 2 years
of being founded.

00:00:27.420 --> 00:00:35.020
Hearing this, you might be thinking that I’m
describing the roaring success of Instagram,

00:00:35.020 --> 00:00:38.140
but this was actually the story of MySpace.

00:00:38.140 --> 00:00:42.560
And the part that we have yet to discuss is
equally explosive downfall.

00:00:42.560 --> 00:00:47.660
In mid 2008, Facebook would surpass MySpace
in terms of user count and within the next

00:00:47.660 --> 00:00:53.770
5 years, MySpace’s user count would crumble
from 115 million to 36 million.

00:00:53.770 --> 00:00:59.040
And the worst part was that MySpace would
be resold to another buyer for just $35 million.

00:00:59.040 --> 00:01:03.080
That’s only 6% of their initial $580 million
buyout.

00:01:03.080 --> 00:01:08.430
And that’s not that surprising given that
virtually no one uses MySpace today.

00:01:08.430 --> 00:01:12.700
On the other hand, Instagram never become
the world’s largest social media platform.

00:01:12.700 --> 00:01:16.909
However, it’s growth was just as explosive
as MySpace.

00:01:16.909 --> 00:01:22.110
Within 3 years of launching, Instagram boasted
an astonishing 100 million users.

00:01:22.110 --> 00:01:27.140
And it didn’t take long for Facebook to
buyout Instagram for a whopping $1 billion.

00:01:27.140 --> 00:01:33.140
But, as we saw with MySpace, rapid adoption
doesn't necessarily indicate long term success.

00:01:33.140 --> 00:01:36.320
And users can dissipate faster than they came
on.

00:01:36.320 --> 00:01:40.190
This isn’t to say that Instagram is going
to explode in spectacular fashion within the

00:01:40.190 --> 00:01:41.580
next couple of years.

00:01:41.580 --> 00:01:46.280
But, at the same time, we’re starting to
see red flags pop up that indicate that Instagram

00:01:46.280 --> 00:01:48.430
may share its final destination with MySpace.

00:01:48.430 --> 00:01:54.369
So, here’s the top reasons that Instagram
is doomed to become the next MySpace.

00:01:54.369 --> 00:01:59.909
YOUNGER DEMOGRAPHIC:
Starting off with the most concrete evidence,

00:01:59.909 --> 00:02:02.300
we have Instagram’s user base.

00:02:02.300 --> 00:02:06.440
While their overall user count is yet to show
any signs of slowing down, something that’s

00:02:06.440 --> 00:02:11.209
worrisome is the demographics of this user
base specifically their age.

00:02:11.209 --> 00:02:15.900
If we take a look at Instagram’s age demographics,
we’ll see that only 8% of their user base

00:02:15.900 --> 00:02:17.970
is 13-17 year olds.

00:02:17.970 --> 00:02:21.310
This means that the number of high schoolers
that are using Instagram is equivalent to

00:02:21.310 --> 00:02:24.680
the number of 45 to 54 year olds that are
using Instagram.

00:02:24.680 --> 00:02:29.480
This may not seem like a problem at first
glance, but when we take a look at their competitors

00:02:29.480 --> 00:02:32.650
demographics, we’ll see just how much Instagram
is lacking.

00:02:32.650 --> 00:02:34.299
Take Snapchat for example.

00:02:34.299 --> 00:02:40.260
13-17 year olds make up just over 20% of their
user base while 18-24 year olds make up nearly

00:02:40.260 --> 00:02:41.260
40%.

00:02:41.260 --> 00:02:47.049
Meanwhile, 50+ year olds make up just 3.7%
which is 8 times less than their 13-17 year

00:02:47.049 --> 00:02:48.049
old user base.

00:02:48.049 --> 00:02:51.939
If we take a look at TikTok, we’ll see a
demographic that’s even more skewed towards

00:02:51.939 --> 00:02:52.939
younger people.

00:02:52.939 --> 00:02:58.329
TikTok’s largest user base is 10-19 year
olds who make up a quarter of their user base.

00:02:58.329 --> 00:03:02.849
Something else to note is that even though
10-19 year olds are their largest demographic,

00:03:02.849 --> 00:03:05.769
TikTok is quite popular amongst other age
groups as well.

00:03:05.769 --> 00:03:10.170
The reason this is a problem for Instagram
is that it’s concrete evidence that they’re

00:03:10.170 --> 00:03:12.760
not appealing to newer generations like they
used to.

00:03:12.760 --> 00:03:16.010
This isn’t to say that teenagers aren’t
using social media nowadays.

00:03:16.010 --> 00:03:19.390
Social media use amongst amongst teenagers
is higher than ever before.

00:03:19.390 --> 00:03:24.120
In fact, 97% of 13-17 year olds use social
media.

00:03:24.120 --> 00:03:26.379
Instagram is simply not their top choice.

00:03:26.379 --> 00:03:30.730
Based on the demographic numbers, they far
prefer SnapChat and TikTok.

00:03:30.730 --> 00:03:35.450
Meanwhile, Instagram’s demographic numbers
are starting to look more and more like Facebook’s.

00:03:35.450 --> 00:03:38.980
Facebook is extremely unpopular amongst 13-17
year olds.

00:03:38.980 --> 00:03:44.280
In fact, there’s more 55-64 year olds that
use Facebook than 13-17 year olds.

00:03:44.280 --> 00:03:48.769
Even the 65+ demographic is comparable to
13-17 year olds at Facebook.

00:03:48.769 --> 00:03:52.569
Now, there are some benefits that come with
an aging demographic.

00:03:52.569 --> 00:03:56.499
First of all, your user base actually has
money to spend meaning that you can charge

00:03:56.499 --> 00:03:58.650
advertisers a much higher amount.

00:03:58.650 --> 00:04:03.269
And secondly, you probably wont have stupid
trends go viral on your platform like devious

00:04:03.269 --> 00:04:04.269
licks.

00:04:04.269 --> 00:04:06.629
But, that’s pretty much where the benefits
end.

00:04:06.629 --> 00:04:10.669
As people get older, they tend to spend less
time on social media not only because they

00:04:10.669 --> 00:04:14.840
have more responsibilities, but also because
they no longer feel the need to live for the

00:04:14.840 --> 00:04:15.840
gram.

00:04:15.840 --> 00:04:19.090
They tend to prioritize family, kids, and
close friends over keeping up some sort of

00:04:19.090 --> 00:04:20.190
online persona.

00:04:20.190 --> 00:04:24.370
While this is probably a good choice for them,
this is a terrible choice for social media

00:04:24.370 --> 00:04:25.370
platforms.

00:04:25.370 --> 00:04:28.760
Your user base slowly evolves from teenagers
and young adults who spend 3-4 hours per day

00:04:28.760 --> 00:04:32.920
on your platform to middle aged people who
check in once every few days or weeks.

00:04:32.920 --> 00:04:36.640
I don’t think I need to explain why this
is terrible for business.

00:04:36.640 --> 00:04:41.260
And unless Instagram starts to get newer generations
onboard, this is where they’re eventually

00:04:41.260 --> 00:04:42.790
headed.

00:04:42.790 --> 00:04:47.630
FADING ORIGINALITY:
Aside from lack luster performance amongst

00:04:47.630 --> 00:04:50.890
Gen Z, Instagram has devolved into becoming
copycats.

00:04:50.890 --> 00:04:55.570
At first, Instagram’s parent company, Meta,
tried to acquire their way to the top.

00:04:55.570 --> 00:04:59.730
They spent ludicrous amounts on acquisitions
like Instagram and WhatsApp.

00:04:59.730 --> 00:05:03.910
But, not every business owner can be persuaded
to sell by just money.

00:05:03.910 --> 00:05:09.560
For example, Facebook offered $3 billion in
cash to takeover SnapChat way back in 2013,

00:05:09.560 --> 00:05:12.880
but SnapChat’s CEO Evan Spiegel refused.

00:05:12.880 --> 00:05:17.010
And when Meta realized they couldn’t acquire
every company they liked, they just started

00:05:17.010 --> 00:05:19.040
ripping off every company they liked.

00:05:19.040 --> 00:05:23.450
We saw Instagram introduce stories which were
awfully similar to Snapchat stories.

00:05:23.450 --> 00:05:27.310
We also saw Instagram launch Reels which were
basically a ripoff of TikTok.

00:05:27.310 --> 00:05:32.621
Now, we can’t give Instagram too much heat
because basically every social media platform

00:05:32.621 --> 00:05:34.080
has resorted to doing this.

00:05:34.080 --> 00:05:37.750
I mean, just take a look at YouTube stories
and shorts.

00:05:37.750 --> 00:05:41.400
The problem with this, however, is that such
shameless copying leaves these platforms with

00:05:41.400 --> 00:05:44.850
no originality as they all basically become
the same thing.

00:05:44.850 --> 00:05:49.440
Not to mention none of these copied features
are all that great at attracting new users.

00:05:49.440 --> 00:05:54.050
They may attract new creators who are looking
to leverage the low competition, but it rarely

00:05:54.050 --> 00:05:55.130
attracts new users.

00:05:55.130 --> 00:06:00.161
I mean, if you don’t have TikTok or Instagram
and you want to watch short form videos, why

00:06:00.161 --> 00:06:04.270
would you download Instagram over TikTok especially
when they’re both free?

00:06:04.270 --> 00:06:05.740
It doesn't make any sense.

00:06:05.740 --> 00:06:09.290
Instagram’s demographic numbers prove this
without a shadow of doubt.

00:06:09.290 --> 00:06:13.790
Meta and YouTube are well aware of this too,
and they’re not trying to attract new users

00:06:13.790 --> 00:06:15.620
with such features per se.

00:06:15.620 --> 00:06:19.560
Rather, they’re trying to preserve their
existing base and minimize losses in watch

00:06:19.560 --> 00:06:20.560
time.

00:06:20.560 --> 00:06:24.540
But, as they spend so much time on copying
features and preserving watch time, they often

00:06:24.540 --> 00:06:27.790
forget about what appealed to users in the
first place.

00:06:27.790 --> 00:06:31.590
This is especially a problem with Instagram
because their user base has already started

00:06:31.590 --> 00:06:32.760
to turn on them.

00:06:32.760 --> 00:06:36.320
And I’m not talking about Meta’s privacy
concerns or political involvement.

00:06:36.320 --> 00:06:40.280
I’m talking about people who are turning
on Instagram because the platform is toxic

00:06:40.280 --> 00:06:41.410
to their mental health.

00:06:41.410 --> 00:06:45.470
It’s no secret that Instagram is filled
with over the top photos.

00:06:45.470 --> 00:06:49.150
Instagram has transitioned from being a place
where you share your life with your friends

00:06:49.150 --> 00:06:52.820
to being a place where you share your highlights
with people you know to being a place where

00:06:52.820 --> 00:06:55.460
you share doctored photos to impress strangers.

00:06:55.460 --> 00:06:59.450
Instagram users are more aware of this than
ever before which has completely warped their

00:06:59.450 --> 00:07:01.600
perception of the platform.

00:07:01.600 --> 00:07:04.500
And I think this is what Meta should have
spent their focus.

00:07:04.500 --> 00:07:08.270
They should have spent time encouraging originality
and authenticity which is what attracted users

00:07:08.270 --> 00:07:10.350
to their platform in the first place.

00:07:10.350 --> 00:07:14.820
But, instead they were busy copying features
from TikTok and SnapChat.

00:07:14.820 --> 00:07:18.760
And as Instagram slowly morphs into being
just another social media platform, it’ll

00:07:18.760 --> 00:07:22.110
just become even harder for them to appeal
to younger generations.

00:07:22.110 --> 00:07:27.940
THE TIKTOK PHENOMENON:
By this point, it’s no secret that one of

00:07:27.940 --> 00:07:32.840
the main factors that’s causing all social
media companies to squirm is TikTok.

00:07:32.840 --> 00:07:37.420
TikTok has taken the world by storm and though
many like to criticize it, TikTok was still

00:07:37.420 --> 00:07:40.170
the most visited website in 2021.

00:07:40.170 --> 00:07:45.450
And given that people only have 24 hours in
a day, all this traffic has to come from somewhere.

00:07:45.450 --> 00:07:49.740
And more times that not, that somewhere is
other social media platforms such as Instagram

00:07:49.740 --> 00:07:51.150
and YouTube.

00:07:51.150 --> 00:07:54.940
And looking forward, it doesn’t seem like
TikTok’s dominance is going to stop anytime

00:07:54.940 --> 00:07:55.990
soon.

00:07:55.990 --> 00:07:59.690
Over the years, our attention spans have only
gotten smaller and smaller.

00:07:59.690 --> 00:08:03.919
First, people switched from traditional media
like movies and TV shows to shorter form online

00:08:03.919 --> 00:08:05.810
content like YouTube videos.

00:08:05.810 --> 00:08:09.520
And now, we’re seeing them switch from YouTube
videos to TikTok shorts.

00:08:09.520 --> 00:08:12.560
This isn’t to say that other forms of media
will be left behind completely.

00:08:12.560 --> 00:08:17.320
But, as TikTok continues its dominance, it’s
likely that other platforms will just continue

00:08:17.320 --> 00:08:21.450
to bleed, but honestly this isn’t anything
new within the social media space.

00:08:21.450 --> 00:08:25.980
Since the creation of social media in the
late 1990s, users have flocked from one platform

00:08:25.980 --> 00:08:27.290
to the next.

00:08:27.290 --> 00:08:28.290
First there was Friendster.

00:08:28.290 --> 00:08:31.600
Then there was Myspace and after that, we
saw Facebook and Twitter.

00:08:31.600 --> 00:08:36.339
At this point, people switched from computers
to smartphones and we saw the rise of Instagram

00:08:36.339 --> 00:08:37.459
and WhatsApp.

00:08:37.459 --> 00:08:39.810
And then, we saw SnapChat and now we have
TikTok.

00:08:39.810 --> 00:08:44.360
None of these platforms stayed at the top
for more than a few years, and they were completely

00:08:44.360 --> 00:08:46.490
abandoned within a few decades.

00:08:46.490 --> 00:08:50.819
Given that Instagram was launched in 2010,
it’s been nearly 12 years since the platform

00:08:50.819 --> 00:08:51.819
was launched.

00:08:51.819 --> 00:08:55.850
So, it’s not surprising that Instagram is
approaching it’s peak form if it’s not

00:08:55.850 --> 00:08:57.329
already there.

00:08:57.329 --> 00:09:01.180
Something else to note is that Meta themselves
have more or less just accepted this fate.

00:09:01.180 --> 00:09:04.990
10 years ago, they were vigorously trying
to acquire the next big platform in order

00:09:04.990 --> 00:09:09.430
to always stay on top, but it seems like Mark
Zuckerberg has come to the realization that

00:09:09.430 --> 00:09:10.900
this simply unsustainable.

00:09:10.900 --> 00:09:14.889
As a result, he’s been shifting the company’s
focus into VR and the metaverse.

00:09:14.889 --> 00:09:19.100
I mean, he even changed the company’s name
from Facebook to Meta which is something you

00:09:19.100 --> 00:09:22.319
never want to do for branding reasons.

00:09:22.319 --> 00:09:26.350
Mark is basically all in on the Metaverse
and he’s even been telling shareholders

00:09:26.350 --> 00:09:30.220
to brace for significant losses due to the
Metaverse over the next 5 years.

00:09:30.220 --> 00:09:34.690
Last year alone, Meta spent $10 billion on
the Metaverse and given Mark’s stance, I

00:09:34.690 --> 00:09:37.439
don’t think this will be changing anytime
soon.

00:09:37.439 --> 00:09:41.790
So, even if Instagram isn’t completely consumed
by newer social media players, it looks like

00:09:41.790 --> 00:09:44.850
Instagram will eventually be left behind by
Meta themselves.

00:09:44.850 --> 00:09:51.450
THE STATE OF INSTAGRAM:
In the end, Instagram is extremely nostalgic

00:09:51.450 --> 00:09:54.040
to many of us because we grew up with it.

00:09:54.040 --> 00:09:57.149
We used it all throughout middle school, high
school, and college.

00:09:57.149 --> 00:10:00.180
And as young adults, many of us still use
it on a regular basis.

00:10:00.180 --> 00:10:04.790
So, it might be hard to imagine this massive
platform slowly wither away.

00:10:04.790 --> 00:10:08.600
But the thing to keep in mind is that all
popular social media platforms crossed this

00:10:08.600 --> 00:10:09.600
same stage.

00:10:09.600 --> 00:10:13.640
MySpace and Friendster were extremely nostalgic
to a specific generation as well.

00:10:13.640 --> 00:10:17.079
But, that didn’t stop these platforms from
eventually going down.

00:10:17.079 --> 00:10:22.490
15 years ago, it probably seemed impossible
for something like MySpace to die, yet here

00:10:22.490 --> 00:10:23.490
we are.

00:10:23.490 --> 00:10:28.240
And as Instagram continues to lose its originality
and Meta shifts their focus onto new projects,

00:10:28.240 --> 00:10:31.920
it just becomes more and more likely that
new generations abandon Instagram.

00:10:31.920 --> 00:10:36.730
We’re already starting to see this amongst
13-17 year olds, but this will simply become

00:10:36.730 --> 00:10:40.540
even more blatant in the next 10-15 years
as these guys grow up.

00:10:40.540 --> 00:10:44.330
And soon enough people will be talking about
Instagram like we talk about MySpace and Friendster

00:10:44.330 --> 00:10:45.330
today.

00:10:45.330 --> 00:10:47.110
But, that’s just what I think.

00:10:47.110 --> 00:10:50.259
Do you think Instagram will break the trend
and survive for decades?

00:10:50.259 --> 00:10:51.529
Comment that down below.

00:10:51.529 --> 00:10:54.730
Also, drop a like if Instagram is nostalgic
for you.

